# The shipped TLS terminator for the remote-index backends.
#
# Same shape and same reason as deploy/embeddings-tls/, one layer over:
# since 2026-08-05 `undercroft-index` refuses cleartext http to any
# non-loopback host with no override (ROADMAP C8), because every push
# carries EMBEDDINGS and an embedding is plaintext-derived data — the
# sealed-vault invariant seals vectors at rest for exactly that reason, so
# shipping them in clear over a network is the same exposure one hop out.
#
# Four HTTP backends terminate here. Caddy's internal CA issues every
# certificate and the root lands on the `undercroft-backends-tls` volume at
# /data/caddy/pki/authorities/local/root.crt; clients mount it read-only
# and pin it with UNDERCROFT_INDEX_CA. The declaration is a PIN — it
# REPLACES the public roots rather than adding to them.
#
# Postgres is not here: it speaks its own protocol, not HTTP, so pgvector
# terminates TLS in the server itself (see the `pgvector` service, which
# runs with `ssl=on` and the same generated key pair). The engine asks for
# it with `sslmode=verify-full` and pins the same root.
#
# Each backend gets its own hostname rather than a path prefix, because the
# backends' own APIs own their paths and a prefix would have to be stripped
# — one more place for a request to be rewritten wrongly.
{
	auto_https disable_redirects
}

https://qdrant-tls {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy qdrant:6333
}

https://chroma-tls {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy chroma:8000
}

https://milvus-tls {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy milvus:19530
}

https://weaviate-tls {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy weaviate:8080
}
